Notes
  - The two balancers are a pair, not a second entry point. One is active
    and one is standby; the failover relationship between them is shown at
    a conceptual level only. No routing protocol is designed here.
  - The request order is: user, balancer, web tier, application tier,
    database primary. Any instance in a tier can be reached from any
    instance in the tier above it.
  - Replication is a separate one-way flow between the two database
    instances. It is not part of the request path.
  - The replica accepts no writes, and nothing here promotes it
    automatically. Database failover remains a manual operation.
  - Two instances per tier are drawn to show the structure. Real counts
    come from measured demand, expected growth, failure tolerance and a
    justified margin, not from this diagram.
  - The firewalls in front of each group and the monitoring system from
    the previous design still apply to every tier here. They are left out
    so that the tier structure stays legible.
  - The rendered version of this design is separated_tiers.png.
